WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.260
Americans are cursing today more

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.350
than ever before.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.600
In fact, the average American utters

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.280
80 to 90 curse words every day.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.740
That's about five curse
words every waking hour.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.170
And it might not be in vain.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.120
Turns out swearing may help you

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.037
live a healthier, happier
life in the long run.

00:00:27.118 --> 00:00:28.270
When you stub your toe

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.960
and holler your favor
dirty, four-letter word;

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.710
you're actually doing yourself a favor.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.580
Swearing has been known
to raise your heart rate,

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.360
which can help reduce the pain.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.680
For example, one study found that people

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.760
who held their hand in icy water

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.500
while cursing lasted 50% longer

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.766
than people who used
neutral words like "wooden."

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:53.833
And "flat."

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.270
And if you're still not convinced

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:58.400
that you should curse more, consider this.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.910
Swearing could be the key
to improving workouts.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.980
Researchers asked people to curse

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.900
while riding a stationary
bike and holding a device

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.770
that measured handgrip strength.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.640
Turns out participants pedaled
faster and gripped stronger

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.420
while spewing their favorite expletives.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.090
And swearing won't just
help you get more fit;

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.140
it can also reduce stress and anxiety.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.630
One study found that swearing
helped drivers better cope

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.460
with their frustration on the road

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.600
whenever a pedestrian
illegally crossed the street.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.740
And, in fact, this kind
of emotional relief

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.890
is so common, it has a name: lalochezia.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.160
Scientists think that
this relief is one reason

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.390
why we've evolved to
curse in the first place

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.020
because it's a way for us
to express strong emotions

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.490
like anger and frustration without having

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.660
to throw a punch or act out.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.670
And this method of choosing words

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.410
over violence has other benefits, too.

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:55.890
Studies show that people
who curse are perceived

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.470
as more genuine and sincere.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.540
And researchers have found that people

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.330
who can list the most swear
words also come across

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.500
as more honest when they're
measured on a lie scale.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.690
But there's still one place

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.113
where cursing is almost always
out of the question: work.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.350
But you might have a good
excuse to swear there, too.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.530
Hey, what the (beeping)!

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.610
Researchers studied a team of workers

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.280
at a soap factory in
New Zealand, and looked

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.321
at the use of one particular swear word.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.471
Um...

00:02:26.517 --> 00:02:28.223
It starts with an F.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.880
It ends with a K.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.050
I think you know which word.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:37.000
Turns out that using the
"f-word" helped workers

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.790
express politeness, alleviate tension,

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.700
and bond with each other.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.950
But we're not saying you should
go and curse out your boss.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.283
Although a little swearing
here and there can't hurt.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.110
I mean (bleeping) it might even help.

